  "worked_solution": "First, to find ${A}^{2},$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${A}^{4}={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
